@startuml game_start_or_end
title Game Start & Game End — Lobby Fill-Up and Match Conclusion

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 2
skinparam roundcorner 5
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA

participant "MatchManager" as MM
participant "Lobby" as L
participant "GameManager" as GM
participant "Controller" as C
participant "PersistenceManager" as PM
participant "ClientHandler\n[all players]" as CH_all
participant "GamePhaseState\n(EndGamePhaseState)" as EGS
participant "RankingDAO" as RDAO

note over MM, GM
  Unlike move/draw/skip/quit, game start and game end are NOT triggered
  directly by an incoming client message: they are side effects fired
  internally by MatchManager once a lobby fills up, and by GameManager's
  own phase state machine once it reaches END_GAME. Both flows are
  transport-agnostic at this level — the final broadcast fans out through
  whichever ModelObserver implementation (ClientHandlerRmi or
  ClientHandlerSocket) each player is using.
end note

== Game Start — Lobby Becomes Full ==

note over MM
  Triggered from MatchManager.joinGame(nickname, id) (RMI ServerRmi.joinGame
  or Socket ClientMessageVisitorImpl.visit(JoinGameMessage)) right after
  lobby.addPlayer(nickname) succeeds.
end note

MM -> L : lobby.checkFullLobby()
L --> MM : true
MM -> MM : scheduler.schedule(() -> startGame(lobby), 0s)
note right of MM
  Scheduled (not called inline) on a single-threaded
  ScheduledExecutorService to avoid races if the lobby
  fills up from two concurrent joinGame() calls; the
  scheduled task re-checks checkFullLobby() before
  actually starting.
end note

MM -> L : lobby.getNicknames() / buildPlayers()
L --> MM : List<String> nicknames\nList<Player> players
MM -> GM : new GameManager(observers, players, capacity,\n  () -> onGameEnded(lobby.getId()))
MM -> C : new Controller(gm, capacity)
MM -> MM : controllers.put(matchId, controller)\ngameManagers.put(matchId, gm)\nlobbies.remove(matchId)

loop for each observer in the now-full lobby
    MM -> CH_all : obs.injectGameVisitor(controller)
end
note right of CH_all
  injectGameVisitor() sets the gameVisitor field used by
  ClientMessageVisitorImpl (socket) purely as an in-game
  guard, and stores the Controller reference each
  ClientHandlerXxx exposes to the message-routing visitor.
end note

MM -> PM : persistenceManager.register(matchId, gm)
MM -> GM : gm.setOnGameStartedCallback(\n  () -> persistenceManager.saveNow(matchId, gm))
MM -> GM : new Thread(gm::initGame).start()
note over MM
  startGame() returns immediately after launching the
  thread; initGame() itself runs asynchronously.
end note

GM -> GM : state.initialize()
GM -> CH_all : notifier.showBoard(state.toDTO(currPhaseState))  [broadcast]
GM -> CH_all : notifier.notifyCurrPlayerUpdate(state.getCurrPlayer().getNickname())  [broadcast]
GM -> GM : onGameStartedCallback.run()\n→ persistenceManager.saveNow(matchId, gm)
note right of CH_all
  Each ClientHandlerRmi/ClientHandlerSocket forwards this
  through sendAsync(): RMI calls clientStub.showBoard(board)
  / clientStub.onCurrPlayerUpdate(nickname); Socket writes
  ShowBoardMessage / CurrPlayerUpdateMessage over TCP.
end note

== Game End — Reaching END_GAME Phase ==

note over GM, EGS
  Triggered from inside GameManager.nextPhase() after the
  last move/draw/skip of the match: when the new phase
  resolves to END_GAME, GameManager fires the state's
  onEntry() hook.
end note

GM -> GM : nextPhase()\n→ currPhaseState = currPhaseState.nextPhase(this)
GM -> CH_all : notifier.notifyPhaseUpdate(currPhaseState)  [broadcast, phase == END_GAME]
GM -> EGS : currPhaseState.onEntry(this)
EGS -> GM : finalScoreCount()
EGS -> GM : getOnGameEndedCallback().run()\n→ MatchManager.onGameEnded(matchId)

GM -> MM : onGameEnded(matchId)
note right of MM
  Runs on the gm::initGame / gm::resume game thread,
  NOT on the RMI/Socket thread that triggered the
  last action — onGameEnded() itself synchronizes
  internally on MatchManager where it touches shared maps.
end note

MM -> GM : gm.calculateRankingPoints()
GM --> MM : Map<Player, Integer> rankingPoints
MM -> MM : numPlayers = controllers.get(matchId).getNumPlayers()\ncontrollers.remove(matchId)\ngameManagers.remove(matchId)\nclientToMatch.entrySet().removeIf(matchId)\npersistenceManager.unregister(matchId)
note right of MM
  unregister(matchId) deletes the match's save file:
  a normally-ended game has nothing left to resume.
end note

note right of MM
  The two database calls are NOT interleaved per player:
  MatchManager.onGameEnded() runs two SEPARATE sequential
  loops over rankingPoints. All insertMatch() calls complete
  first, and only then does the second loop run
  reportPlayerPlace() for every player. This guarantees each
  player's own freshly-inserted score is already visible in
  the DB when ranking positions are computed.
end note

loop for each player in rankingPoints
    MM -> RDAO : RankingDAO.insertMatch(matchId, nickname, score, numPlayers, today)
    note right of MM
      Individually try/caught: a DB error for one
      player is logged, but does not abort the loop
      for the others.
    end note
end

loop for each player in rankingPoints
    MM -> RDAO : RankingDAO.reportPlayerPlace(nickname, numPlayers)
    RDAO --> MM : globalPos
    MM -> MM : globalPositions.put(nickname, globalPos)
    note right of MM
      Individually try/caught: a DB error for one
      player is logged and that player's globalPos
      falls back to -1, but does not abort the loop
      for the others.
    end note
end

MM -> MM : postMatch.put(nickname, numPlayers)  [for every player]
note right of MM
  Moves every player into the post-game state, which is
  what later allows MatchManager.requestRanking(nickname)
  and MatchManager.quit(nickname) [post-game branch] to
  recognise them. Executed inside a synchronized block
  before resetGameVisitor() is called.
end note

loop for each player
    MM -> CH_all : handler.resetGameVisitor()
end
note right of CH_all
  resetGameVisitor() sets gameVisitor back to null on
  each handler, so any further move/draw/skip message
  from that client is rejected as InvalidTimingException.
  Called after postMatch.put(), outside the synchronized block.
end note

MM -> GM : gm.notifyGameEnding(globalPositions)
GM -> GM : finalRanking = rankingCalculator.calculateFinalRanking(...)\nstatsList = players.map(toStatsDTO)\nrankingPositions built from finalRanking
GM -> CH_all : notifier.notifyGameEnding(statsList, globalPositions, rankingPositions)  [broadcast]
note right of CH_all
  Per-listener: each player receives THEIR OWN
  rankingPos/globalPos via onGameEnding(statsList,
  rankingPos, globalPos) — RMI: clientStub.onGameEnding(...);
  Socket: GameEndingUpdateMessage.
  On the client side this also flips gameEnded = true,
  which is what unlocks Client.requestRanking().
end note

@enduml